WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.179
What independent evidence shows, and the caveat on each.

2
00:00:03.459 --> 00:00:04.269
Arena.

3
00:00:04.549 --> 00:00:08.880
At the time of review, the Arena’s agent leaderboard put Claude Fable 5.

4
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.232
2 first overall, followed by Claude Opus 5.

5
00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:16.160
5 and Gemini 4 Carbon, and listed Fable 5.

6
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.317
2 first in web development.

7
00:00:18.597 --> 00:00:21.392
Arena measures human preference on real prompts.

8
00:00:21.672 --> 00:00:30.141
Caveat: the Arena team’s own analysis shows length and formatting sway votes, and providers can test private variants before release.

9
00:00:30.421 --> 00:00:31.915
Artificial Analysis.

10
00:00:32.195 --> 00:00:37.464
It combines a benchmark mix into indices and measures speed and price across endpoints.

11
00:00:37.744 --> 00:00:40.475
At the time of review it ranked Claude Fable 5.

12
00:00:40.755 --> 00:00:47.901
2 first across its capability categories, with Gemini 4 Carbon second in several and Claude Opus 5.

13
00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:51.147
5 and GPT-6 Astra close behind.

14
00:00:51.427 --> 00:01:00.621
Caveat: the indices are averages over benchmarks that may not resemble your work, and blended prices assume a token mix that may not match yours.

15
00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:02.736
SWE-bench Pro and METR.

16
00:01:03.016 --> 00:01:07.773
These are the most relevant independent signals for coding agents (lesson 2).

17
00:01:08.053 --> 00:01:20.939
Caveat: SWE-bench Pro’s grader reliability has been disputed, and METR’s horizon page stopped updating in September 2026, so the newest models have no METR horizon.

18
00:01:21.219 --> 00:01:22.541
What this adds up to.

19
00:01:22.821 --> 00:01:37.669
At the frontier, the top few models from Anthropic, Google, and OpenAI are close enough that rankings flip between leaderboards and months, and the gaps are often smaller than the differences in price (a factor of two or more between flagships,

20
00:01:37.949 --> 00:01:41.981
and up to about 100 times between a flagship and a small tier).

21
00:01:42.261 --> 00:01:55.723
That is the strongest argument for this lesson’s method: when the public evidence says “these three are close,” the tie-breakers are your task, your price, your data terms, and your latency, which only your own eval measures.
